hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"26945","Abu al-Qasim Hibatullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn al-Husayn al-Shaybani informed us, he said: Abu Ali al-Husayn ibn al-Mudhhab narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr Ahmad ibn Jafar ibn Hamdan ibn Malik al-Qutii narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, from Firas, from al-Shaabi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: Fatimah came walking as if her walk were the walk of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Welcome to my daughter, then he seated her on his right or on his left, then he confided a report to her and she wept. I said to her: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) singled you out with his report then you weep. Then he confided a report to her and she laughed. I said: I never saw like today joy nearer to grief. I asked her about what he said, and she said: I would not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, I asked her, and she said: He confided to me and said: Jibril, peace be upon him, used to review the Quran with me every year once, and this year he reviewed it with me twice, and I see only that my term has come, and you are the first of my household to join me, and what an excellent predecessor I am for you. So I wept for that. Then he said: Are you not pleased to be the chief of the women of this ummah or the women of the believers. She said: So I laughed for that."
"26946","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad informed us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fell ill, he called his daughter Fatimah and spoke secretly to her, and she wept, then he spoke secretly to her and she laughed. I asked her about that, and she said: As for when I wept, he informed me that he would die, so I wept, then he informed me that I am the first of his family to join him, so I laughed."
"26947","Yaqub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, from his mother Umm Sulayman, and both were trustworthy, she said: I entered upon Aishah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and asked her about the meat of sacrifices. She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had forbidden it, then he permitted it. Ali ibn Abi Talib came from a journey, and Fatimah brought him meat of her sacrifices, and he said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not forbid it. She said: He has permitted it. She said: So Ali entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that, and he said to him: Eat them from Dhu al-Hijjah to Dhu al-Hijjah."
"26948","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym, narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Hasan, from his mother Fatimah daughter of Husayn, from her grandmother Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, he invoked blessings on Muhammad and salutation, and said: O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy, and when he went out, he invoked blessings on Muhammad and salutation, then said: O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your bounty. Ismail said: So I met Abdillah ibn Hasan and asked him about this hadith, and he said: When he entered he said: My Lord, open for me the door of Your mercy, and when he went out he said: My Lord, open for me the door of Your bounty."
"26949","He said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Layth narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah daughter of Husayn, from her grandmother Fatimah daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, he said: In the name of Allah, and peace upon the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy, and when he went out, he said: In the name of Allah, and peace upon the Messenger of Allah, O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your bounty."
"26950","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from his father, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me and ate a bone with meat, then Bilal came with the call to prayer, and he stood to pray, so I took his garment and said: O father, will you not perform ablution. He said: From what should I perform ablution, O daughter. I said: From what fire touched. He said to me: Is not the best of your food what fire touched."
"26951","Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan, meaning Ibn Salih, narrated to us, from Layth, from Abdillah ibn al-Hasan, from Fatimah daughter of Husayn, from Fatimah daughter of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: When he entered the mosque, he invoked blessings on Muhammad and salutation, then said: O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your mercy, and when he went out, he invoked blessings on Muhammad and salutation, and said: O Allah, forgive me my sins and open for me the doors of Your bounty."
"26952","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad, meaning Ibn Rashid, narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, he said: Fatimah entered upon Abu Bakr and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed me that I am the first of his family to join him."
"26953","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali said to us: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote to me to copy to him the will of Fatimah, and in her will was the curtain which people claim she introduced, and that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to her, and when he saw it he returned."
"26954","Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, Zamah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, he said: Fatimah used to bounce al-Hasan ibn Ali and say: By my father, the likeness of the Prophet, not resembling Ali."
